  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Massachusetts has $245M in federal contract obligations in FY2027 to date. The state has 8,265 awards with an average award size of $29.6K. Obligations fell 99.0% year over year. Fiscal history shows obligations were $18.4B in FY22, $20.3B in FY23, $19B in FY24, $21.4B in FY25, and $23.5B in FY26. The Department of Veterans Affairs is the top buying agency in FY2027 to date with $115M, followed by the Department of the Treasury with $36.6M and the Department of Transportation with $31M. CRANE & CO., INC. is the top vendor in FY2027 to date with $36M, followed by RAYTHEON COMPANY with $14.5M and PROGENICS PHARMACEUTICALS INC with $12.8M. Paper Mills is the largest industry by obligations in FY2027 to date with $34M, followed by Engineering Services with $27.8M and Commercial and Institutional Building Construction with $27.6M. All figures are contract obligations; current-year totals are partial (fiscal year to date).",
